"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, drdr.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. The DLL for RE Framework will be downloaded inside the game's folder, along with the DRDR Mod, which will be placed in the 'reframework' folder.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"DRDR is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'drdr.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, The RE Framework mod loader windows will appear. The default key to manually open the windows should be 'INSERT' but you can change it in the Configuration tab.\n\nInside the Archipelago Client for REFramework window:\n\nIn the 'Host' field, enter archipelago.gg: followed by the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nIn 'Slot', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nFinally, click the Connect button and then, you can start a new run!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for RE7 AP Client.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear' option it will delete everything related to REFramework and mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
